keel-core (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The manifest names the installation modes of Core and lets Core be the
    witness of cloud advanced (handbook decision 0076): modes: [simple,
    cloud_simple, cloud_advanced] and witness: true. The first boot's Role
    screen offers Witness only on an appliance that says so, and keel
    0.23.83 is the first that reads both keys, so keel (>= 0.23.83) is a
    dependency: an older keel refuses them as unknown.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 23:36:02 +0000

keel-core (0.1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Core carries the service VIP overlay (handbook decision 0049: every
    replicated pair gets a VIP, databases, Keel Web pairs and WordPress
    alike), like the wireguard and etcd overlays (0029). keel-overlay-vip
    (>= 0.1.1, the first that ships its units off) joins the dependencies
    and the manifest names it disabled in every mode; keel enables it on a
    node whose spec declares appliance.vip. keel (>= 0.20.0), the first that
    knows it.

 -- KeelLinux maintainers <admin@keellinux.org>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 23:25:09 +0000

keel-core (0.1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The banner picks the machine's public address (#24): the version the
    core layer of the attended release of 2026-10-03 carries.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 04:26:41 +0000

keel-core (0.1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Monit starts after the units of Core's processes, ssh.service,
    webmin.service and postfix.service: a drop-in,
    /usr/lib/systemd/system/monit.service.d/keel-core.conf, ordering only.
    Started beside them, monit's first cycle after a boot found webmin and
    postfix inactive (Keel-Linux/keel#61, item 2). keel writes no
    `set daemon ... with start delay` instead: that line is global, and
    keel leaves the operator's cycle alone (decision 0021).

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 06:00:00 +0000

keel-core (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First release (handbook decision 0041, first implementation, step 4).
    Ships the appliance manifest of Keel Core from docs/manifest-v1.md as
    /usr/share/keel/appliances/core.yaml: installer enabled in every mode,
    wireguard and crowdsec disabled in simple and enabled in the cloud
    modes, etcd enabled in cloud advanced only; sshd, Webmin and postfix
    as its processes, with the ssh, HTTPS and SMTP probes. The format's
    web shell (shellinabox, 12320) is left out: TurnKey removed it in
    18.0, the image has no unit for it, and a manifest naming one fails
    keel manifest validate on the machine (handbook errata of 0041).
  * Depends on keel-overlay-installer, keel-overlay-wireguard,
    keel-overlay-etcd and keel-overlay-crowdsec, and on keel (>= 0.13.0),
    the first keel that converges the overlays and writes Monit's checks
    from the manifests.

 -- Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0000
